This weeks video is a venture in to ASMR again but this time we're going with Ice Cream Cookie Sandwiches!

We've gone with Double Chocolate cookies and Red Velvet Cookies, they are perfect with a slight gooey centre and loaded with chocolate chips. 

For the ice cream, we've gone with heavenly white chocolate ice cream with a slight boozy kick from some Mozart white chocolate liqueur ;).....you're welcome!

What do you need?

Cookies:
Cookies Recipe:
* 150g Butter , softened
* 200g Sugar
* 1 Egg
* 1 tsp vanilla extract
* 200g flour
* 1 tsp  baking soda
* 25g  cocoa powder (double chocolate)
* 100g Milk Chocolate chips (double chocolate)
* Red Food Colouring (red velvet)
* 8g cocoa powder (red velvet)
* White Chocolate Chips (red velvet)

Instructions
- Preheat oven to 175c/350f degrees.
- In a large bowl, cream together butter and sugar and beat until smooth.
- Beat in egg, then stir in the vanilla.
- Combine flour, baking soda, and salt; stir into the creamed mixture until just blended. Divide the mix in 2 and add the 25g cocoa and milk chocolate chips to one half. Add the red food coloring, 8g of cocoa and white chocolate chips to the other half. Put them in the fridge for 2-3 hours. 
- Make 2” rounds and place on a covered cookie sheet
- Bake for 12-15 mins
- Cool completely

For the White Chocolate Ice Cream:
435ml Milk
450ml Cream @40%
70g Sugar
60g Dextrose
40g Golden syrup
35g SMP
50g White Chocolate 
30ml Mozart White Chocolate liqueur

Warm the milk, sugars & SMP slightly then add the white chocolate and stir until melted. Take off the heat, add the cream, then chill in the fridge over night. 
White chocolate often semi solidifies in the fridge so be prepared to get busy with an emersion blender or whisk before churning. 

